# Git Commit Rules

## Format

`type(scope): description`

- Use lowercase English only.
- Write a subject line only, with no body.
- Do not add trailers such as `Co-Authored-By` or `Signed-off-by`.

## Types

`feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `chore`, `docs`, `style`, `test`, `perf`, `ci`,
`build`

## Scopes

- Use `root` for repository-wide files and `image-view` for
  `packages/pi-image-view`.
- For a future `packages/pi-<name>` workspace, remove the `pi-` prefix to
  derive its scope.
- Prefer `scope/module`, such as `image-view/clipboard`,
  `image-view/gallery`, or `root/biome`.
- Use `root/agents` for `AGENTS.md`, `.agents/**`, and agent-specific adapters.
- Use a bare scope only when a change genuinely spans multiple modules in it.
- For cross-scope changes, use comma-separated bare scopes only:
  `chore(root,image-view): update test tooling`.

## Type-specific scope rules

- Use `docs(root)` for top-level documentation and `docs/**`.
- Use the package scope for package documentation, such as
  `docs(image-view): update usage instructions`.

## Commit ordering in multi-commit plans

Plan commits in dependency order, with `docs` commits first.

## Examples

- `feat(image-view/clipboard): support animated image paste`
- `fix(image-view/gallery): preserve preview order`
- `chore(root/agents): add git commit rules`
- `build(root): update bun workspace config`
